<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer says sees no more big layoffs.</title>
<headline>Sulzer says sees no more big layoffs.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-10-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sulzer AG chief executive Fritz Fahni said he did not envisage any more major job cuts at the engineering group along the lines of a recent restructuring at weaving unit Sulzer Rueti.</p>
<p>&quot;Restructuring is needed always and everywhere,&quot; he said in an interview with the Finanz und Wirtschaft newspaper published on Saturday. &quot;But steps like those we just announced for Sulzer Rueti are not immiment.&quot;</p>
<p>Sulzer Rueti said this week it would cut nearly a third of its 3,200 jobs and take a charge of up to 36 million Swiss francs that will lower 1996 group profit at Sulzer AG.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
